{#- Role Prompting -#}
You are a senior test engineer. Annotate this Selenium test with @AccessMode for each shared Resource it touches.

{#- Few-Shot/In-Context Learning and Use of delimiters -#}
=== CATALOG ===
{{ resourcefile }}

=== EXAMPLES ===
{{ examples }}

=== TARGET TEST ===
{{ testcase }}

=== ACCESS MODES ===
READONLY: only reads.
READWRITE: reads and modifies.
NOACCESS: no interaction.
DYNAMIC: creates/destroys at runtime.
concurrency: max parallel tests (int >= 1).
sharing: true if the instance may be shared concurrently.

=== TASK ===
{#- Chain-of-Thought -#}
Think step by step: list method calls in the test -> match each to a catalog Resource -> choose accessMode/concurrency/sharing.
Missing Resources go in proposed_resources; never annotate them.
{#- Re-reading -#}
Re-read once more and drop any annotation not backed by a specific line.
Rules: only catalog Resources; collapse conflicts to READWRITE; at least one annotation per test.

{#- Be Clear and Precise -#}
=== OUTPUT (start with the JSON fence, no preamble) ===
```json
{"test_method":"<name>","resources":[{"resource":"<catalog name>","access_mode":"<READONLY|READWRITE|NOACCESS|DYNAMIC>","evidence_line":"<code line>"}],"proposed_resources":[{"name":"<name>","explanation":"<why>"}]}
```
```java
@AccessMode(resID="<resource>", concurrency=<N>, sharing=<true|false>, accessMode="<READONLY|READWRITE|NOACCESS|DYNAMIC>")
```
